{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.FieldTheory.RatFunc.AsPolynomial","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.RationalRoot"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubic_no_ratFunc_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubic_no_ratFunc_root","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L183-L198","doc":"**No rational-function root** (Gauss). A root `f ∈ K(z)` of the monic\n`C_z(X)` is integral over `K[z]`; `K[z]` is integrally closed, so `f` is a\npolynomial, and `colorCubicAt_ne_zero` bites. Hence `C_z(X)`, a cubic with no root\nover the field `K(z)`, is irreducible there: **no colour sheet is a rational\nfunction of `z`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_eval₂_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_eval₂_poly","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L176-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_eval₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_eval₂","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L169-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly_monic","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L165-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicPoly","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L160-L163","doc":"The colour cubic as a **monic** polynomial over `K[z]`: the outer variable is\nthe colour coordinate, the inner `X` is `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L147-L156","doc":"**The colour cubic has no polynomial root in `z`** (characteristic zero):\n`C_z(r) ≠ 0` for every `r ∈ K[z]`. With Gauss's lemma (monic over the integrally\nclosed `K[z]`) this is irreducibility of `C_z(X)` over `K(z)`: no colour sheet\nis a rational function of `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_ne_zero_of_two_le_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_ne_zero_of_two_le_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L109-L145","doc":"**No root of degree `≥ 2`.** The leading term `r³` has degree `3d`, strictly\nabove `1 + 2d`, `2 + d` and `3`, so `C_z(r)` has degree `3d > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_linear_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_linear_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L79-L107","doc":"**No affine root.** For `r = a z + b` the coefficient system is inconsistent:\nthe `z³` coefficient forces `a = −1` or `a² = −1`, and in each branch the `z²` and\n`z⁰` coefficients contradict each other (`5 = 0`, resp. `65 = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt_linear","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L68-L77","doc":"The four `z`-coefficients of `C_z(az + b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicIrreducible.colorCubicAt","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicIrreducible.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The colour cubic `C_z(X)` evaluated at `X := r ∈ K[z]`; the polynomial\nvariable `X` of `K[X]` plays the role of the base coordinate `z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}